# @PROJECT_NAME@ — agent guide

RayWaves project. Gameplay is C++ in `@SOURCE_DIR@/`, compiled to
`GameLogic.dll`. Scenes are INI files in `@ASSET_DIR@/<MapId>.scene`.

## Tooling

`rwcli` lives in the RayWaves package, not in this folder. Run the generated
wrapper from the project root:

```powershell
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd doctor . --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd info . --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd maps . --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd build . --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd run . --frames 120 --screenshot shot.png --state state.json --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd scene list . --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd lsp . --check --json
.\.raywaves\bin\rwcli.cmd validate . --json
```

If the wrapper is missing or stale, read `.raywaves\tooling.ini` and use
`[rwcli] path`. If `available=0`, the package CLI was not found; build the
`rwcli` target or ask the user. Do not guess the package location.

PowerShell: quote paths with spaces, and add `2>$null` when capturing JSON to
suppress informational stderr lines.

Full command reference: `.agents/skills/raywaves-game/reference.md`.

## Loop

1. `doctor` — toolchain, manifest, scenes, lock.
2. Edit `@SOURCE_DIR@/*.cpp`. Gameplay stays there; never edit `.raywaves/`.
3. `build --json` — fix every `diagnostics[]` entry, then build again.
4. `run --json` — inspect `screenshot.nonEmpty`, `entities[]`, `state`.
5. Repeat.

## API cheatsheet

```cpp
#include "rw.h"

class MyLevel : public rw::Level
{
public:
    MyLevel() : rw::Level("MyLevel") {}

protected:
    void OnStart() override
    {
        m_Texture.Load("player.png");                         // @ASSET_DIR@/player.png
        m_Player = Spawn("Player", { 320, 240 }, { 48, 64 }, rw::Origin::Center);
        Cam().SetZoom(1.0f);
    }

    void OnUpdate(float dt) override
    {
        if (rw::IsKeyDown(KEY_RIGHT)) { m_Player->position.x += 240.0f * dt; }
        Cam().Follow(m_Player->position, dt);
    }

    void OnDraw() override { rw::DrawSprite(m_Texture, *m_Player); }

private:
    rw::Texture m_Texture;
    rw::Entity* m_Player = nullptr;
};

RW_GAME(MyLevel)
```

- `rw::Game` + `AddLevel<T>("id")` for multiple levels.
- `Spawn(name, position, size, origin)` registers with the editor and `rwcli state`.
- `rw::IsKeyDown` / `rw::IsKeyPressed` / `rw::IsMouseButtonDown` are replayable
  by `rwcli run --input script.txt`. Raw `IsKeyDown` still works but is not
  scriptable.
- Input script: `frame,KEY_RIGHT,down` / `frame,KEY_RIGHT,up`, one per line.
- Assets resolve relative to `@ASSET_DIR@/`.

## Rules

- All gameplay code in `@SOURCE_DIR@/`. No gameplay in the engine.
- `RW_GAME(...)` exactly once per project.
- Do not edit `.raywaves/`; it is generated.
- Asset names: `A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -`.
- Scene files: prefer `rwcli scene ...`; hand-editing is allowed, keys are
  `id,name,texture,position,rotation,scale,source,tint,layer,visible`.
- Close the editor before scene edits, or rely on the agent lock.

## Failure recovery

- `build_failed`: read `diagnostics[]`; `file`, `line`, `column` point at the
  compiler message. `rawTail` has the last build lines.
- `abi_mismatch`: rebuild GameLogic with the current engine.
- `run_crashed`: the game process died; `logs` in the error contains stderr.
- `run_timeout`: raise `--timeout` or lower `--frames`.
- `build_locked`: another build owns `.raywaves/agent.lock`; wait or
  `rwcli doctor --fix`.

